d into parcel-level retail service availability or measured performance."],[3,"Consumer price guidance and contract rights do not establish which package is orderable or active at an individual parcel."],[4,"A discussion paper, qualitative evidence or national improvement objective is not an observed signal or speed measurement at a parcel."],[5,"Proposed spectrum authorisations for ships and aircraft do not demonstrate terrestrial broadband or mobile availability at a land parcel."],[6,"Modernisation commitments and migration principles do not prove that a particular parcel has completed fibre migration or retains emergency power resilience."],[7,"Call-handling compliance guidance does not provide parcel coverage, provider availability, speed or fixed-network technology evidence."],[8,"National switch-off schedules and device guidance do not prove current 4G or 5G signal quality at a specific parcel."],[9,"A voluntary switch-off charter is not evidence that replacement coverage or device compatibility has been verified at an individual parcel."],[10,"Fault troubleshooting advice and customer reports are not independently measured parcel signal, availability or speed data."],[11,"A provider enforcement decision does not establish service availability, network technology, price or speed at any parcel."],[12,"Complaint escalation rights and ADR membership do not prove parcel-level service quality or correct any coverage record."],[13,"Provider-level complaint rates are aggregate indicators and cannot be assigned to a parcel or used as measured connectivity."],[14,"Compensation eligibility and payments do not establish actual parcel coverage, speed or fault duration without validated address-level evidence."],[15,"Quarterly provider complaint statistics do not identify service conditions or measured performance at an individual parcel."]],"web_visibility":{"explicit_row_numbers":true,"latest_rows_visible":120},"source_count_inflation_prevented":true,"fake_data":false,"db_write":false,"migration":false,"production_deploy":false}